The five petaloid sepals of the flower can be oriented divergent from or perpendicular to the floral axis.{{rp|49}}{{rp|376}} These sepals are ovate to ovate-lanceolate in shape, coming to acute tips. The sepals of a flower are shorter than its petals, measuring between {{cvt|15|mm}} and {{cvt|30|mm}} long and {{cvt|6|mm}} to {{cvt|16|mm}} wide. The inner structure of the flowers form a cup-like appearance.{{rp|204}}
